---
import ProsePage from '../../templates/ProsePage.astro';
import ContactForm from '../../components/ContactForm.astro';
import NewsletterForm from '../../components/NewsletterForm.astro';
import Tabs from '../../components/Tabs.astro';
import { routePath } from '../../i18n/routes.ts';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL, PRETALX_CFP_URL, REPO_URL, releaseName } from '../../config/site.ts';

const release = releaseName('001');
const openCallMail = `mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}?subject=Open%20call%20${release}`;
---

<ProsePage
  locale="en"
  routeKey="contribute"
  title="Contribute"
  description="Four routes: a story on stage, a room, a field report, or an event you know about. None of them costs money."
>
  <p>
    This community is made of whatever people put into it. Below are the four routes that exist
    today, and exactly what each one asks for. Not sure which is yours? Mail
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. One sentence is plenty.
  </p>

  <Tabs
    id="routes"
    label="Ways to contribute"
    tabs={[
      { id: 'speak', label: 'Speak' },
      { id: 'venue', label: 'Offer a room' },
      { id: 'fieldnote', label: 'Field report' },
      { id: 'listing', label: 'List an event' },
    ]}
  >
    <div id="speak" data-tabs-panel>
      <h2 data-tabs-heading>Tell people something at {release}</h2>
      <p>
        The evening opens with two roughly half-hour talks: one concrete thing you built, fixed or
        broke, and what you took away from it. No deck full of logos, no product pitch, no "the
        future of". Speaking experience is not required. A real story about a real system is the
        only criterion.
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>About half an hour, questions included. Dutch or English, either is fine.</li>
        <li>The subject does not matter as long as you did the work yourself.</li>
        <li>Who gets on stage is decided by the open call, on the same terms for everyone.</li>
      </ul>
      {
        PRETALX_CFP_URL ? (
          <p>
            <a class="button button--primary" href={PRETALX_CFP_URL} rel="noopener">
              Submit your talk
            </a>
          </p>
        ) : (
          <p>
            The open call currently runs by e-mail: send three sentences on what it is about to{' '}
            <span>
              <a href={openCallMail}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>.
            </span>
            If there are more proposals than slots, the call moves to a public submission tool with
            availability and review. It is ready, and it opens when it adds something.
          </p>
        )
      }
    </div>

    <div id="venue" data-tabs-panel>
      <h2 data-tabs-heading>Offer a room</h2>
      <p>
        A release needs space for forty people, with food and drinks. That is the most valuable
        thing a company can contribute and the first thing we ask for. In-kind support always comes
        before money here. What you get for it, and what you explicitly do not buy, is on
        <a href={routePath('companies', 'en')}>companies</a>.
      </p>
      <ContactForm
        id="host"
        to={CONTACT_EMAIL}
        subject="Offering a room for a twente.dev release"
        submitLabel="Send"
        fallbackLabel="Mail us"
        note="Sending opens your own mail app with this message in it. Nothing goes to an external service."
        fields={[
          { name: 'org', label: 'Organisation', required: true },
          { name: 'contact', label: 'Name and e-mail address', required: true },
          { name: 'city', label: 'Town in Twente', required: true },
          { name: 'capacity', label: 'How many people fit, seated?', required: true },
          {
            name: 'offer',
            label: 'What can you offer: room, food, both, something else?',
            type: 'textarea',
            required: true,
          },
          { name: 'when', label: 'Which months would suit you?', type: 'textarea' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>

    <div id="fieldnote" data-tabs-panel>
      <h2 data-tabs-heading>Tell your story in a field report</h2>
      <p>
        A field report is an interview. We ask the questions, write down the answers and turn that
        into a report, so there is no writing for you to do. Put yourself forward as a subject, or
        point us at someone building something here that the rest of Twente can learn from. After
        that it lives in the <a href={routePath('blog', 'en')}>archive</a>, so it stays findable.
      </p>
      <ContactForm
        id="fieldnote-form"
        to={CONTACT_EMAIL}
        subject="Proposing a field report"
        submitLabel="Send"
        fallbackLabel="Mail us"
        note="Sending opens your own mail app with this message in it. Nothing goes to an external service."
        fields={[
          { name: 'name', label: 'Name and e-mail address', required: true },
          { name: 'subject', label: 'What is it about?', required: true },
          {
            name: 'lesson',
            label: 'What is the lesson? One or two sentences is enough',
            type: 'textarea',
            required: true,
          },
          { name: 'language', label: 'Dutch or English?' },
        ]}
      />
    </div>

    <div id="listing" data-tabs-panel>
      <h2 data-tabs-heading>List an event or a community</h2>
      <p>
        Everything on this site is a file in a public repository, so a submission is an issue or a
        pull request. Pick whichever you find easier:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>An event</strong>: open to the public and relevant to developers.
          <a href={`${REPO_URL}/issues/new/choose`}>Open the form</a>, or add the file yourself. It
          appears in the calendar and the ICS feed straight away.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>A community</strong>: Discord, Slack, user group or meetup. We do not list anyone
          without asking, so preferably submit your own group;
          <a href={routePath('communities', 'en')}>the directory</a> explains how that works.
        </li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        Found something broken or wrong? <a href={REPO_URL}>Open an issue</a>. The full step-by-step
        is in <a href={`${REPO_URL}/src/branch/main/CONTRIBUTING.md`}>CONTRIBUTING</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </Tabs>

  <h2>Stay in the loop</h2>
  <p>
    Contributing does not have to start today. One email when the {release} programme is set, one when
    registration opens, and the field reports after that. That way you can see the kind of story that
    lands here before you send one in yourself.
  </p>
  <NewsletterForm locale="en" id="contribute-updates" />

  <h2>Supporting us</h2>
  <p>
    There is deliberately no donate button here. What we need is a room, food, people who turn up
    and someone willing to tell a story. All of that can be offered above. If an organisation wants
    to back a release financially, that is a conversation rather than a rate card: mail
    <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>. A payment route arrives only once there
    is something to fund that cannot be given in kind, and it arrives with a public account of it.
  </p>
</ProsePage>
